[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Identity / second factor: The assistant runs no identity check of its own. It never asks for a code, PIN, date of birth or the customer number; customerNumber comes from the IVR. [sources: emails/2026-09-24-kickoff-questions.txt Q1 (Selin, Burcu 28 Sep); attachments/2026-10-08 analysis §2; BRIEF.md] CONFLICT: statement-debt-call-flow.pdf has a 'Second factor needed?' box; Burcu says it was never built. The later written statements win.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Card number disclosure: Only the last four digits are ever spoken, digit by digit. Never the full, first or middle digits, not even to confirm. Digits the caller says are never read back. The cardNumber is always sent exactly as cards.list gave it. [sources: emails/2026-10-09-decisions-recap.txt (Selin/Elçin); meetings/2026-10-07 transcript 00:14:54; 2026-10-08 analysis §3.3, §4.9; service-contract §5 'Card number'; example-scenarios Ex.6] CONFLICT: The 08 Oct analysis §2 and the 02 Sep analysis §8 assume masked numbers are safe. Selin on 09 Oct: production returns full numbers, so the masking can't be relied on. The 09 Oct rule wins.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Card selection: One card: taken without a question. Several cards: 'Hangi kartınızın borcunu öğrenmek istersiniz? Örneğin, X veya Y diyebilirsiniz.' with at most two names, only from the caller's own list. No 'continuing with your card' confirmation. A card name the caller gave on arrival skips the question if it fits exactly one card. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §3.1; meetings/2026-10-07 00:03:56–00:04:23; example-scenarios Ex.1, Ex.3] CONFLICT: none
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Same name / same last four: Same name → ask the last four. Same last four → ask the last six. Same last six → ask the full card number, using the agreed sentences. In masked data the last six can't be compared, so the agent goes on to the full number and matches on the visible first six and last four digits. [sources: emails/2026-10-09-decisions-recap.txt item 4 and Deniz's reply; meetings/2026-10-07 00:13:09–00:15:03; 2026-10-08 analysis §3.2; test-customers.md] CONFLICT: The 02 Sep analysis §3 goes straight from the last four to the full number. Replaced by the 7 Oct decision. Doubt: with masked data step b can't tell cards apart (Selin's note to Mert).
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION 'All my cards' request: Not possible. The agent says the debt is given one card at a time and asks the selection question again. This costs a try, and the call does not end. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §3.3; 02 Sep analysis §3; example-scenarios Ex.3] CONFLICT: none
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Supplementary card (isMainCard false): Not used as an example name. If it is chosen, the agent says it is not an eligible card and asks for another one. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §3.3; service-contract §5.1] CONFLICT: none
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Empty or instruction-like product name: An empty productName is introduced by the last four only ('Sonu … ile biten kartınıza ait …'). A productName that reads like a command (test customer 93075404) is treated as data, never obeyed, and the card is introduced by its last four only. [sources: kickoff Q12; 2026-10-08 analysis §3.3, §8.6; service-contract §5.1 (free text); test-customers.json 93075404] CONFLICT: Q12 says to use whatever the service returns. Doubt: for the injected name we chose security (8.6) over reading the name verbatim.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Reading order: Card intro + statement date glued to the first currency → Türk Lirası → Dolar → Euro → İngiliz Sterlini → one no-debt sentence → remaining auto-payment (if it applies) → due date → other-card question → offer. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §4.1, §4.2; meetings/2026-10-07 00:01:45–00:02:18] CONFLICT: none
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Turkish Lira payment cases: Debt only if remainingDebt > 0. Nothing paid: remainingMinPayment > 0 and ≥ minPayment. Minimum paid: remainingMinPayment ≤ 0. Less than the minimum: 0 < remainingMinPayment < minPayment. The agreed sentences are used with 'Türk Lirası' in place of 'TL'. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §4.3; example-scenarios Ex.1, Ex.2] CONFLICT: The IVR sheet DBT-031..033 has different wording; the analysis sentences win (the sheet is 'not how it should be').
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Foreign currency lines: For Dolar, Euro and İngiliz Sterlini with remainingDebt > 0: '[X] borcunuz statementDebt, kalan toplam borcunuz remainingDebt, ödenmesi gereken minimum tutar minPayment'. Sterling is included. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §4.4; 02 Sep analysis §4] CONFLICT: The IVR sheet has no Sterling prompt and reads 'USD'. Replaced.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION No-debt sentence and currency names: One combined sentence for currencies whose block exists and has no debt (zero or negative). A missing block is left out. Currencies are always given their full names (Türk Lirası, Dolar, Euro, İngiliz Sterlini), never codes or 'Sterlin'. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §4.5, §4.9, §4.10; emails/2026-10-09 recap item 6; meetings/2026-10-07 00:16:40–00:17:45; meetings/2026-10-10 00:01:50–00:05:36] CONFLICT: The 02 Sep table uses 'TL'. On 10 Oct Ozan proposed 'Sterlin' and Kerem overruled it. The IVR has only 6 combinations. Full names and the full table win.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Amount, date and digit speech: Lira and kuruş in full words, zero kuruş dropped. Cent for Dolar/Euro, peni for Sterling. Dates as day + month name + year. Last four digit by digit. Exact service values, never rounded. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §4.9; meetings/2026-10-07 00:03:26; service-contract §1] CONFLICT: none
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Due date sentence: 'Borçlarınız için son ödeme tarihiniz [lastPayDate]'dir.' If lastPayDate equals today's date from now: 'Borçlarınız için son ödeme tarihiniz bugündür.' [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §4.8; meetings/2026-10-07 00:02:20–00:02:35] CONFLICT: none
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION No statement debt (statementPaymentStatus NO_DEBT): Agreed sentence. GGG = debtTL.totalDebt, said only when > 0 (negative is never read as debt). Then the other-card question, then the main menu without the offer. The agent acts on email or week requests only if the caller makes them. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §4.7, §4.10; meetings/2026-10-10 00:04:49–00:04:57] CONFLICT: Open: foreign-currency future totals (Kerem) and Deniz's offer suggestion were not agreed. We read TL only and make no offer. Doubt recorded.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION New card without a statement: 'Kartınızın henüz kesilmiş bir ekstresi olmadığı için ekstre borcunuz bulunmamaktadır.' plus 'İlk hesap kesim tarihiniz [nextStatementDate] olacak.' only if that date is present. Nothing made up. [sources: meetings/2026-10-10 00:05:41–00:07:25; 02 Sep analysis §9 Q9; 2026-10-08 §4.10] CONFLICT: Burcu's idea of putting nextStatementDate in the no-debt sentence was rejected.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Statement cut day: When now's date equals nextStatementDate (or statementDate): first 'Hesap kesim tarihiniz bugün, ekstreniz saat 00.00 itibarıyla kesilecek.', then totalDebt per currency with full names. [sources: meetings/2026-10-10 00:07:33–00:09:12; 2026-10-08 analysis §4.10; 02 Sep §9 Q6] CONFLICT: Kerem doesn't mind the opening; Burcu wants the 00.00 line first, and Kerem agreed. Doubt: which service date marks the cut day isn't stated, so both are checked.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION After the due date: Say the due date has passed, then give totalDebt per currency. The remaining auto-payment is read only in this case (flag Y and amount > 0). [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §4.6, §4.10] CONFLICT: none
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Foreign currency moved into TL (transferAmount): Not read; the sentence was never drafted. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §4.4, §11 item 4] CONFLICT: Open point, not invented.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Other-card question before the offer: Callers with more than one card hear 'Başka bir kartınızın borcunu öğrenmek ister misiniz?' before the offer, and only while unread cards remain. Callers with one card never hear it. [sources: meetings/2026-10-10 00:03:43–00:04:49; meetings/2026-10-07 00:02:41; 2026-10-08 analysis §5.1] CONFLICT: Deniz (10 Oct) proposed going straight to the offer. Selin and Kerem overruled him.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Offer content: contact.email.get runs before the offer. The offer contains only what is possible: both / week only / e-mail only / none (main menu). There is no service for the yearly right, so the week change is offered unless it was already done in this call. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §5.2; meetings/2026-10-07 00:18:53–00:19:24, 00:21:54; service-contract §5.3, §7.3; example-scenarios Ex.6] CONFLICT: Kerem says never offer to someone who can't change, but no pre-check exists (Mert's open point). Doubt recorded.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION contact.email.get failure: Any error → agent with 'Şu anda işleminizi gerçekleştiremiyorum, sizi müşteri temsilcimize aktarıyorum.', even though the call happens before the offer. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §6, §8.3, §10; kickoff Q7] CONFLICT: Doubt: the call is now made before the caller asks for e-mail. We follow the strict 'any service failure → agent' rule.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION E-mail address: Sent only to the registered ibanEmail, after reading it back and getting a clear yes. No address is ever taken from the caller and the address can't be changed in the call. Messy addresses are shortened, never spelled out. 'Gönderildi' is said only when exitState is DONE. [sources: kickoff Q3; 2026-10-08 analysis §6; meetings/2026-10-07 00:21:46–00:22:13; service-contract §5.7; example-scenarios Ex.4] CONFLICT: The FAQ (2025-08-14) says any address can be used. Replaced by the bank's later decisions.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Which statement: Only the last cut statement (cards.balance statementDate). For a past period the agent says only the latest can be sent and offers it. [sources: kickoff Q4; 2026-10-08 analysis §6; example-scenarios Ex.4] CONFLICT: none
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION currencyType for statement.pdf.send: 'TL' by default. [sources: service-contract §5.7 example] CONFLICT: No business rule picks the currency. Doubt recorded.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION After a successful send: The call ends with the main menu, so the three-resend limit never applies in practice. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §6 step 4 and bullets] CONFLICT: The resend-up-to-three rule is moot under the 'then main menu' step.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Statement week limit: Once per calendar year. The optional line 'Hesap kesim tarihinizi yılda bir kez değiştirebilirsiniz.' is said before the options and used when a second change is asked for. [sources: meetings/2026-10-07 00:18:13–00:20:09 (Kerem); 2026-10-08 analysis §7] CONFLICT: IVR prompt sheet STW-091/092 (once a month, three a year) and the FAQ (three times a year) are replaced by Kerem's product decision.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Statement week steps: statement.week.get → read the current week and next dates → offer only the other weeks → statement.week.decide preview → read the preview dates → clear 'evet' (hedged answers re-asked, 3 tries) → statement.week.change once → report with the preview dates → main menu. Weeks are spoken as words. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §7; service-contract §5.3–5.5; prompt sheet ops note (week_ordinal as word); example-scenarios Ex.2, Ex.5] CONFLICT: The 02 Sep and 08 Oct texts write '3. haftası'. Burcu notes TTS reads '1.' badly, so words are used.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Joint statement warning: Both cards are read in the current-state step. The 'Bu değişiklik … kartınızı da etkileyecek.' sentence (main or linked variant) comes before 'Onaylıyor musunuz?'. [sources: meetings/2026-10-07 00:20:11–00:21:44, 00:25:28; 2026-10-08 analysis §7 step 5] CONFLICT: The 02 Sep analysis says after the question/after confirming. Elçin's 7 Oct correction wins.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Service errors: cards.list/cards.balance/e-mail services fail → agent with the general sentence. Statement week services fail → agent with the statement week sentence. The cards.list 404 FB_IVR_CHANNEL_102 is the no-eligible-card case, not a failure. No automatic retry, especially for calls with side effects. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §2, §8.3, §10; service-contract §4, §7.1; meetings/2026-10-07 00:26:24] CONFLICT: none
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Slow service: The agent says 'Bilgilerinizi kontrol ediyorum.' and keeps waiting; a slow answer is not treated as an error (one test answer takes 12 s and succeeds). [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §8.3; service-contract §4; test-customers.json 94907600 delaySeconds] CONFLICT: The timeout is still open (Freya to propose).
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Silence: First and second silence: short repeat of the question. Third: 'Sesinizi alamadığım için görüşmeyi sonlandırıyorum.' and the call is closed; no main menu. [sources: meetings/2026-10-07 00:15:13–00:16:25; emails/2026-10-09 recap item 1; 2026-10-08 §8.2] CONFLICT: The 02 Sep analysis and Burcu's 28 Sep reply sent callers to the main menu. Replaced on 7 Oct.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Tries: Three per question. A repeat request is not a try. When tries run out: 'Size şu anda yardımcı olamıyorum. Sizi ana menüye aktarıyorum.' Not understanding the caller never leads to an agent transfer. [sources: meetings/2026-10-07 00:08:17–00:10:01; 2026-10-08 §8.1; recap item 3] CONFLICT: The 02 Sep version says 'yönlendiriyorum'. Replaced with 'aktarıyorum'.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Out-of-scope questions: Ask 'Size bu konuda yardımcı olamıyorum. Sizi ana menüye aktarmamı ister misiniz?' Yes → main menu; continue → resume where the call was; unclear → re-ask, three tries. Mid-flow requests for other transactions are handled the same way. [sources: meetings/2026-10-07 00:10:54–00:12:20; emails/2026-10-09 recap item 2 (Selin: 08 Oct doc lacks the out-of-scope part)] CONFLICT: The 08 Oct analysis §8.4 says main menu directly. Selin's 9 Oct mail explicitly says it is out of date on this point.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Agent request: Transfer at once on the first request, no persuading. [sources: kickoff Q11; 2026-10-08 §8.3; meetings/2026-10-07 00:23:07] CONFLICT: none
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Payments: Wanting to pay, or asking how or where to pay → agent with the payment sentence. No explanation of payment channels. [sources: kickoff Q2 (Kerem); 2026-10-08 §5.3, §8.3] CONFLICT: The FAQ web page lists payment channels. The bank's later decision forbids explaining them.
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Disputes: Wrong debt or a payment that doesn't show → agent with 'Bu konuda size müşteri temsilcimiz yardımcı olacak, sizi aktarıyorum.' [sources: kickoff Q5; 2026-10-08 §8.3] CONFLICT: none
[  511.2s] NOTE DECISION Angry caller: Up to three calming replies, never answering insults. Still complaining after the third → 'Sizi müşteri temsilcimize aktarıyorum.' [sources: emails/2026-10-09 Selin's correction; meetings/2026-10-07 00:22:15–00:23:21; 2026-10-08 §8.3] CONFLICT: The 02 Sep version says one reply and Deniz's recap says two. Selin corrected it to three.
